From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:19:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 022/342] power: meson_scpi, CPU temperature and clock on the
 Amlogic GXBB

A device-manager driver for the firmware's legacy SCPI protocol on the
Meson GXBB (S905): commands go to BL30 through the MHU mailbox in the
HIU block, payloads through shared SRAM (polled, one command in flight,
100 ms timeout; after a timeout it stops sending, since the same
firmware serves PSCI).

/dev/power/meson_scpi/0 reads as text: temperature (aml_thermal, whole
degrees C), the CPU operating points and the current one. Writing
"<MHz>", "max" or "auto" sets the clock, only when the driver settings
contain "dvfs on" (the C2's device tree disables its SCPI clock node);
it never goes above 1536 MHz, the boot clock. "auto" follows the busiest
CPU (above 80 % the top point, below 30 % one point down, floor 1000
MHz), and in every mode the temperature limits the clock from 80 C.

Tested on the ODROID-C2: 42-49 C; operating points 100-1536 MHz; a
fixed busy loop takes 14.6 s at 1536, 22.5 s at 1000 and 45.1 s at
500 MHz; auto idles at 1000 and goes to 1536 under load; reboot still
works; a 10-minute network/disk stress run was clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
